include: "<stddef.h>"
include: "mixa_manager/mixa_backend_headless.h"

# Header unit for the clean L2 port of mixa_backend_headless (share-
# and-backends ticket 20260913-192700, module 6 of 6, the LAST module
# in the standing list). mixa_backend_headless.h is real, plain, hand-
# written C (like mixa_backend.h/mixa_pump.h before it) -- no L1 .h.
# lm1 counterpart exists anywhere in this codebase. Nothing to predef
# here, only the real header itself (which itself plain-includes the
# real mixa_backend.h and mixa_event_fifo.h), reached the exact same
# zero-cost `include:`-not-`predef:` way the real mixa_backend_
# headless.lm1 already does. MixaHeadless's own fields are
# dereferenced via `\` in the real body with no L1-level struct:
# declaration for MixaHeadless/MixaBackend/MixaEventFifo anywhere,
# proven safe by the established "`\` defers to gcc" finding from
# ticket 20260913-151000 (mixa_app_controller). Total distinct
# predef'd files: 0.
